<title>UK: Typhoon threatens ships in western Pacific -WSC.</title>
<headline>Typhoon threatens ships in western Pacific -WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Marie, with 75 mph winds, is a significant threat to shipping in the open waters of the western Pacific near 18.1n/159.8e, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp (WSC) said.</p>
<p>Marie was upgraded to typhoon status by WSC overnight.</p>
<p>It is moving north at 10 mph. This track will continue while Marie strengthens during the next 36 hours.</p>
</text>
